      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T19:14:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e which is why we cannot just remember this pointer in struct pkvm_pgtable, and need to pass it around instead\n\nBTW I imagine we could avoid passing it around: since we eventually feed the pages from the memcache to the per-VM pool (in guest_mmu_put_page()) anyway, we could just do that right away, i.e. in admit_host_page(). Thus guest_mmu_zalloc_page() would just always allocate from the per-VM pool instead of the memcache.\n\nI guess the only reason not to do that is the unneeded overhead of attaching the page to the pool in hyp_put_page() -\u003e __hyp_attach_page() every time.",
      "parentUuid": "0f1ce9ea_412842c1",
      "revId": "d8cd595401ec40e98bfb84c648b7fa45d7ab59be",
